# Read by `pnpm --filter @prl/api test:without-database` via node's --env-file.
#
# It exists as a file rather than an inline `PRL_TESTS_WITHOUT_DATABASE=1 node ...` assignment in
# the package script because an inline assignment depends on which shell pnpm spawns, and the one
# thing this flag must not do is silently fail to apply.
#
# What it means: the caller has said out loud that this run will not exercise SQL. The database
# suites skip, `test/database-availability.test.ts` prints a banner saying the run proves nothing
# about SQL, and the waiver is IGNORED when CI is set — see test/helpers/database.ts.
#
# node's --env-file never overrides a variable that is already in the environment, so a shell that
# exports DATABASE_URL still gets the database suites; the waiver only tolerates their absence.
PRL_TESTS_WITHOUT_DATABASE=1
